{"id":"freertos","corpus":"aws","title":"FreeRTOS","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/freertos/latest/userguide/what-is-freertos.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"FreeRTOS"},{"kind":"p","text":"Developed in partnership with the world's leading chip companies over a 15-year period, and now downloaded every 170 seconds, FreeRTOS is a market-leading real-time operating system (RTOS) for microcontrollers and small microprocessors. Distributed freely under the MIT open source license, FreeRTOS includes a kernel and a growing set of libraries suitable for use across all industry sectors. FreeRTOS is built with an emphasis on reliability and ease of use."},{"kind":"p","text":"FreeRTOS includes libraries for connectivity, security, and over-the-air (OTA) updates. FreeRTOS also includes demo applications that show FreeRTOS features on qualified boards."},{"kind":"p","text":"FreeRTOS is an open-source project. You can download the source code, contribute changes or enhancements, or report issues on the GitHub site at https://github.com/FreeRTOS/FreeRTOS."},{"kind":"p","text":"We release FreeRTOS code under the MIT open source license, so you can use it in commercial and personal projects."},{"kind":"p","text":"We also welcome contributions to the FreeRTOS documentation (FreeRTOS User Guide, FreeRTOS Porting Guide, and FreeRTOS Qualification Guide). To view the markdown source for the documentation, see https://github.com/awsdocs/aws-freertos-docs. It's released under the Creative Commons (CC BY-ND) license."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Sign up for an AWS account"},{"kind":"p","text":"To get started with AWS, you need an AWS account. For information about creating an AWS account, see Getting started with an AWS account in the AWS Account Management Reference Guide."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Download FreeRTOS source code"},{"kind":"p","text":"Download the latest FreeRTOS and Long Term Support (LTS) packages from the Downloads page on freertos.org."},{"kind":"h2","text":"FreeRTOS-qualified hardware platforms"},{"kind":"p","text":"The following hardware platforms are qualified for FreeRTOS:"},{"kind":"li","text":"ATECC608A Zero Touch Provisioning Kit for AWS IoT"},{"kind":"li","text":"Cypress CYW943907AEVAL1F Development Kit"},{"kind":"li","text":"Cypress CYW954907AEVAL1F Development Kit"},{"kind":"li","text":"Cypress CY8CKIT-064S0S2-4343W Kit"},{"kind":"li","text":"Espressif ESP32-DevKitC"},{"kind":"li","text":"Espressif ESP-WROVER-KIT"},{"kind":"li","text":"Espressif ESP-WROOM-32SE"},{"kind":"li","text":"Espressif ESP32-S2-Saola-1"},{"kind":"li","text":"Infineon XMC4800 IoT Connectivity Kit"},{"kind":"li","text":"Marvell MW320 AWS IoT Starter Kit"},{"kind":"li","text":"Marvell MW322 AWS IoT Starter Kit"},{"kind":"li","text":"MediaTek MT7697Hx Development Kit"},{"kind":"li","text":"Microchip Curiosity PIC32MZEF Bundle"},{"kind":"li","text":"Nordic nRF52840-DK"},{"kind":"li","text":"NuMaker-IoT-M487"},{"kind":"li","text":"NXP LPC54018 IoT Module"},{"kind":"li","text":"OPTIGA Trust X Security Solution"},{"kind":"li","text":"Renesas RX65N RSK IoT Module"},{"kind":"li","text":"STMicroelectronicsSTM32L4 Discovery Kit IoT Node"},{"kind":"li","text":"Texas Instruments CC3220SF-LAUNCHXL"},{"kind":"li","text":"Microsoft Windows 7 or later, with at least a dual core and a hard-wired Ethernet connection"},{"kind":"li","text":"Xilinx Avnet MicroZed Industrial IoT Kit"},{"kind":"p","text":"Qualified devices are also listed on the AWS Partner Device Catalog."},{"kind":"p","text":"For information about qualifying a new device, see the FreeRTOS Qualification Guide."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Additional resources"},{"kind":"p","text":"These resources might be helpful to you."},{"kind":"li","text":"For additional FreeRTOS Documentation, see freertos.org."},{"kind":"li","text":"For questions about FreeRTOS for the FreeRTOS engineering team, you can open an issue on the FreeRTOS GitHub page."},{"kind":"li","text":"For technical questions about FreeRTOS, see the FreeRTOS Community Forums."},{"kind":"li","text":"For more information about connecting devices to AWS IoT, see Device Provisioning in the AWS IoT Core Developer Guide."},{"kind":"li","text":"For technical support for AWS, see AWS Support."},{"kind":"li","text":"For questions about AWS billing, account services, events, abuse, or other issues with AWS, see the Contact Us page."}],"lemmas":{"developed":["developed","develop"],"developeds":["developeds","developed"],"develops":["develops","develop"],"developing":["developing","develop"],"partnerships":["partnership","partnerships"],"world's":["world"],"worlds":["world","worlds"],"leading":["leading","lead"],"leadings":["leading","leadings"],"leads":["lead","leads"],"leaded":["leaded","lead"],"led":["led","lead"],"chips":["chip","chips"],"chipping":["chipping","chip"],"chipped":["chipped","chip"],"companies":["company","companies"],"years":["year","years"],"periods":["period","periods"],"downloaded":["downloaded","download"],"downloadeds":["downloadeds","downloaded"],"everies":["everies","every"],"seconds":["second","seconds"],"markets":["market","markets"],"marketed":["marketed","market"],"marketing":["marketing","market"],"reals":["real","reals"],"times":["time","times"],"timed":["timed","time"],"timing":["timing","time"],"operating":["operating","operate"],"operatings":["operatings","operating"],"operates":["operates","operate"],"operated":["operated","operate"],"systems":["system","systems"],"microcontrollers":["microcontrollers","microcontroller"],"smalls":["small","smalls"],"smaller":["smaller","small"],"microprocessors":["microprocessor","microprocessors"],"distributed":["distributed","distribute"],"distributeds":["distributeds","distributed"],"distributes":["distributes","distribute"],"distributing":["distributing","distribute"],"freelies":["freelies","freely"],"opens":["open","opens"],"opened":["opened","open"],"opening":["opening","open"],"sources":["so